# Conformance probe pack for `when` lists and ranges (spec 0.20) on a fixed
# `bits` layout, least significant bit first. Public.
#
#   byte 0   x, common; it is also the bits of every kind's `when`
#   byte 1   by kind
#     lo    when 1,3..5    y
#     hi    when 4..9,20   z       4 and 5 are lo's too: lo is first (ruling 2)
#     dup   when 30,30     w       a value repeated in one list loads
#
# x covers exactly the bits of the `when`: on encode x is written when the
# entity holds x and its value matches the kind's list, else the first value
# is (rulings 3 and 15). x has the default 4, which is in lo's list: a default
# does not count (ruling 15), so lo without x writes 1.
format     conformance-kinds-bits
version    0.20.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
default probe.x  4
field  probe.x  0:0:8  uint
kind   lo
when   0:0:8  1,3..5
requires probe.y
field  probe.y  0:8:8  uint
kind   hi
when   0:0:8  4..9,20
requires probe.z
field  probe.z  0:8:8  uint
kind   dup
when   0:0:8  30,30
requires probe.w
field  probe.w  0:8:8  uint
